revert data (`Contracts.UniswapV2.ERC20.Slice.Post`, which imports only `Verify.Shapes` and
`Verify.Spec.HashScope`). Every predicate of the specification is written out here.

`runtimeBytes` is the runtime bytecode solar printed (`--emit bin-runtime` with
`Certified/uv2_erc20/options`) for the same flattened file solc's AST was read from, in the run
that produced this module (Certified/uv2_transfer_e6/MANIFEST.md).

`Statement` is two instances of `Generic.Expected` over those bytes, with the caller a parameter:

* `specAny`: every real caller (below `2 ^ 160`, not the contract), every well-formed
  `transfer(to, v)` with no value from any storage writing the constructor's slot. Postcondition:
  the source's sequenced updates sent by the caller, unconditionally, and the target property
  `TargetPostAt` wherever the call's finite footprint is Keccak-separated.
* `specScoped`: every real caller whose own footprint is separated; valid calls carry the finite
  footprint premise `ScopedSep (transferFootprint 1 caller to)`; postcondition `TargetPostAt`.

`TargetPostAt a` states, for the caller `a`: `a ≠ to` succeeds iff `s[a] ≥ v` and `s[to] + v` does
not overflow, then debits `a` and credits `to`; the self-transfer `a = to` succeeds iff `s[a] ≥ v`
and changes no storage; a success logs `Transfer(a, to, v)`, returns `true` and writes no other
slot; a failure reverts with SafeMath's revert data, no log, no change. Overflow and the
self-transfer are cases the statement decides, not assumptions. Gas: from 8199112 on, the bytes'
observable is the source's (observable equality, not a no-out-of-gas claim).
-/

